From e04bd7abb0d3c5fb6bfcdcbc665ba9b807f8d013 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-agent <arena-agent@local>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 12:30:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Record one setup step per line
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The first report with a timeline in it printed every step twice — once as
STILL RUNNING and once with a duration — because the store kept a step's begin
and its end as two entries and the timeline printed each entry as it came.

recordEvent now folds an end into the open entry for the same step, and the
timeline also collapses a paired begin and end if it is handed one. Only the
trailing open entry folds, so a signer rebuilt mid-session appends a fresh
machine.open instead of editing the cost recorded for the first.

Correcting something said alongside the previous commit: stuckInStep was never
wrong. A step's begin and end carry the same label and the same start
timestamp, so scanning back to either gives the same answer — feeding the
report's own event list to the deployed build returns exchange.1, which is what
the report said. The timeline duplicated; the conclusion above it was right.
The runningStep change made for that misreading has been dropped.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
